# Line-ending policy for this repository.
#
# Why this file exists (finding m9 of the 2026-10-07 audit): core.autocrlf was
# true and there was no .gitattributes, so the working tree mixed CRLF and LF
# (62 of the text files were CRLF). `gofmt -l .` therefore reported 76 files as
# unformatted — almost all of it pure EOL noise — which made gofmt useless as a
# gate and buried the 10 files with REAL formatting drift.
#
# The default is LF for every text file, stated explicitly rather than left to
# `* text=auto` (which converts to the NATIVE ending on checkout, i.e. CRLF on
# this host, and would put the tree straight back out of sync with
# scripts/normalize-eol.mjs). Only the Windows script types keep CRLF.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.vbs text eol=crlf
# Binary artifacts must never be normalized or diffed as text.
*.dll  binary
*.exe  binary
*.so   binary
*.h    binary
*.zip  binary
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.ico  binary
